Ace, we have positive contact.

356
00:25:58,240 --> 00:25:59,908
That's our target! Get us down!

357
00:25:59,992 --> 00:26:01,076
Daddy!

358
00:26:01,201 --> 00:26:03,036
- Daddy!
- Baby, get back.

359
00:26:03,245 --> 00:26:04,580
Daddy!

360
00:26:04,663 --> 00:26:05,664
Gerry?

361
00:26:05,747 --> 00:26:07,332
- Gerry, what?
- Stay back!

362
00:26:07,416 --> 00:26:08,834
Baby! No!

363
00:26:08,917 --> 00:26:10,252
One thousand seven.

364
00:26:10,335 --> 00:26:11,837
One thousand eight.

365
00:26:11,920 --> 00:26:13,589
Daddy, get off the edge!

366
00:26:13,672 --> 00:26:16,091
- Gerry, please?
- One thousand ten.

367
00:26:18,010 --> 00:26:19,761
One thousand eleven.

368
00:26:25,559 --> 00:26:27,227
I got it in my mouth.

369
00:26:27,519 --> 00:26:29,730
You're okay. You're okay.

370
00:26:31,690 --> 00:26:33,275
Go! Go!

371
00:26:36,403 --> 00:26:37,821
Come on. Come on.

372
00:26:46,288 --> 00:26:47,456
Let's go! Let's go!

373
00:26:47,748 --> 00:26:49,583
Come on, let's go! We got to go!

374
00:26:54,004 --> 00:26:55,172
You got her?

375
00:27:07,976 --> 00:27:09,770
Let's go, let's go, let's go!

376
00:27:32,584 --> 00:27:35,420
Traffic en route, altitude 5-7 thousand.

377
00:27:35,504 --> 00:27:39,091
Heading 250. Turn right,
heading 075, once clear.

378
00:27:40,008 --> 00:27:41,760
Remain below 4,000.

379
00:27:56,275 --> 00:28:00,570
Clear to land,
heading 040, wind 060 at five.

380
00:28:02,072 --> 00:28:05,200
Follow L.S.O. directions.
Prep for immediate dust off.

381
00:28:28,307 --> 00:28:29,516
Gerry.

382
00:28:29,683 --> 00:28:31,059
Thank you.

383
00:28:31,143 --> 00:28:33,145
Good to see you, my friend.

384
00:28:33,228 --> 00:28:34,980
Tango five, this is Argus command.

385
00:28:35,063 --> 00:28:36,231
Cleared for take-off.

386
00:28:36,481 --> 00:28:38,400
Tango five. Wilco.

387
00:28:57,377 --> 00:28:58,628
Karin, to the right.

388
00:28:58,879 --> 00:29:00,422
This is good, right?

389
00:29:00,505 --> 00:29:02,174
Bunk beds!

390
00:29:02,257 --> 00:29:05,218
Your bunk beds
are number two, three and six.

391
00:29:05,552 --> 00:29:06,762
Please make yourself at home.

392
00:29:06,845 --> 00:29:08,263
You want to get up here?

393
00:29:09,014 --> 00:29:11,850
- There you go, sweetheart.
- That's good.

394
00:29:11,933 --> 00:29:13,727
We're not dropping anchor again.

395
00:29:14,227 --> 00:29:15,354
You're safe.

396
00:29:15,437 --> 00:29:16,521
It's not me I'm worried about.

397
00:29:16,605 --> 00:29:18,065
They're safe.

398
00:29:18,732 --> 00:29:20,108
Baby.

399
00:29:21,443 --> 00:29:23,987
It's bigger than
our old apartment on 72nd.

400
00:29:25,238 --> 00:29:26,406
Need anything, Karin?

401
00:29:26,948 --> 00:29:27,991
Water.

402
00:29:28,658 --> 00:29:29,701
I'll organize.

403
00:29:31,453 --> 00:29:33,705
Is this worldwide?
Is anyone doing better than we are?

404
00:29:34,915 --> 00:29:37,125
Baby. Go talk somewhere else.

405
00:29:37,793 --> 00:29:38,919
Okay.

406
00:29:48,095 --> 00:29:49,304
The President is dead.

407
00:29:50,639 --> 00:29:53,308
Four of six Joint Chiefs. V.P. missing.

408
00:29:53,892 --> 00:29:56,728
Reports of gun battles
in the streets of the capital.

409
00:29:56,812 --> 00:29:57,979
Your parties are panicking.

410
00:29:58,939 --> 00:30:00,440
The bigger cities are the worst off.

411
00:30:00,524 --> 00:30:03,485
The airlines
were the perfect delivery system.

412
00:30:04,736 --> 00:30:08,031
Carnival cruise vessel Dream
has been given permission to join.

413
00:30:08,281 --> 00:30:10,826
Twenty seven knots south and closing.

414
00:30:11,159 --> 00:30:13,161
How soon are they showing
symptoms after contact?

415
00:30:13,328 --> 00:30:15,080
The provisional
government currently considers

416
00:30:15,163 --> 00:30:16,623
northern Minnesota
to be a potential safe zone.

417
00:30:16,706 --> 00:30:18,417
Have you recorded
any instance where a person

418
00:30:18,500 --> 00:30:20,001
was bitten but not infected?

419
00:30:25,715 --> 00:30:27,551
How the hell do I know
if Russia's fallen?

420
00:30:32,180 --> 00:30:34,141
Sir, I cannot action that order.

421
00:30:34,224 --> 00:30:35,934
Colonel, I'm sorry,
but we cannot facilitate

422
00:30:36,017 --> 00:30:37,853
an evacuation for you or your men.

423
00:30:38,145 --> 00:30:41,148
Sir, there is nowhere to evacuate you to.

424
00:30:41,898 --> 00:30:43,984
Malnutrition. Dirty water.

425
00:30:44,609 --> 00:30:46,528
No gas for the winter or transportation.

426
00:30:47,028 --> 00:30:48,780
No bullets to fight.

427
00:30:48,864 --> 00:30:50,532
And it has spread
to all corners of the globe.

428
00:30:50,699 --> 00:30:52,075
The question
that we have got to address

429
00:30:52,200 --> 00:30:53,452
is what the hell is it?

430
00:30:53,535 --> 00:30:55,787
About 5% of the population
aren't affected immediately.

431
00:30:55,871 --> 00:30:59,708
It is viral. It has to be viral.
There is no plausible alternative.

432
00:31:00,041 --> 00:31:03,962
And like any virus, once we find its
origin, we can develop a vaccine.

433
00:31:04,045 --> 00:31:06,715
- We find it, contain it...
- That's Dr. Fassbach.

434
00:31:07,340 --> 00:31:08,633
Virologist from Harvard.

435
00:31:08,717 --> 00:31:11,178
The analogy I keep coming back to

436
00:31:11,428 --> 00:31:12,721
is Spanish Flu.

437
00:31:12,888 --> 00:31:13,930
Spanish Flu?

438
00:31:14,055 --> 00:31:16,099
It didn't exist in 1918, but by 1920,

439
00:31:16,183 --> 00:31:18,143
it killed 3% of the world.

440
00:31:18,351 --> 00:31:21,605
He's our best bet
at figuring out what this thing is.

441
00:31:22,063 --> 00:31:23,565
You all read the same email I did,

442
00:31:23,899 --> 00:31:26,610
and it said "zombies."

443
00:31:26,693 --> 00:31:28,987
Are you completely out of your mind?

444
00:31:29,070 --> 00:31:31,615
So, the earliest mention
of the word "zombie"

445
00:31:31,698 --> 00:31:34,493
was ina memo
from Camp Humphreys in South Korea.

446
00:31:34,743 --> 00:31:36,328
We haven't had contact with them since.

447
00:31:36,411 --> 00:31:37,787
But this could lead us to the origin.

448
00:31:37,871 --> 00:31:39,623
If we knew where this thing started,

449
00:31:39,706 --> 00:31:42,792
then we'd have a chance
of developing a vaccine to stop it.

450
00:31:42,876 --> 00:31:45,712
So we send in Dr. Fassbach
there to look for the source.

451
00:31:45,795 --> 00:31:47,297
He's just a kid.

452
00:31:48,256 --> 00:31:49,341
You're right.

453
00:31:50,258 --> 00:31:51,760
Attention on deck!

454
00:31:56,306 --> 00:31:57,432
At ease!

455
00:32:00,435 --> 00:32:02,270
Mr. Under-Secretary.

456
00:32:04,439 --> 00:32:05,774
The Under-Secretary
here says you were

457
00:32:05,857 --> 00:32:08,527
his best investigator
when you were at the U.N.

458
00:32:08,610 --> 00:32:11,029
I want to send you in. With a team.

459
00:32:11,112 --> 00:32:14,115
Help Dr. Fassbach
find whatever it is he needs.

460
00:32:14,866 --> 00:32:15,867
You brought...

461
00:32:15,951 --> 00:32:17,953
I wanted for the circumstances
to speak for themselves.

462
00:32:18,036 --> 00:32:19,120
No.

463
00:32:20,622 --> 00:32:22,791
Captain, I'm not your guy.

464
00:32:23,833 --> 00:32:26,920
You were on the ground
during the Liberian Civil War.

465
00:32:27,128 --> 00:32:30,715
Investigated Chechen war crimes.
Sri Lanka in '07.

466
00:32:30,966 --> 00:32:33,760
Places you and I both know
Dr. Fassbach wouldn't last a night in.

467
00:32:33,843 --> 00:32:36,304
Gerry, a handful of SEALs
will go with you as security force.

468
00:32:36,388 --> 00:32:37,430
No.

469
00:32:37,514 --> 00:32:39,599
My guys will get you in,
you assist the doctor,

470
00:32:39,683 --> 00:32:41,726
pursue any leads,
my guys will get you out.

471
00:32:42,185 --> 00:32:43,645
We do the heavy lifting.

472
00:32:44,521 --> 00:32:47,816
I can't help you. I can't leave my family.

473
00:32:50,026 --> 00:32:51,987
Take a look around here, Mr. Lane.

474
00:32:52,487 --> 00:32:56,741
Each and every one of these people are
here because they serve a purpose.

475
00:32:58,326 --> 00:33:01,496
There's no room here
for non-essential personnel.

476
00:33:01,871 --> 00:33:03,206
There's a long line of people

477
00:33:03,331 --> 00:33:05,083
waiting for one of those bunks.

478
00:33:07,669 --> 00:33:09,546
You want to help your family,

479
00:33:09,671 --> 00:33:12,299
let's figure out how we stop this.

480
00:33:13,008 --> 00:33:15,010
It's your choice, Mr. Lane.

481
00:33:15,343 --> 00:33:16,511
Simple.

482
00:33:19,055 --> 00:33:20,473
You don't work for them anymore.

483
00:33:20,557 --> 00:33:21,975
- Karin...
- You might not remember

484
00:33:22,058 --> 00:33:24,144
what this job did to you, but I do.

485
00:33:24,227 --> 00:33:26,187
So do not ask me to say yes to this.

486
00:33:26,271 --> 00:33:27,314
I have to go.

487
00:33:28,398 --> 00:33:30,150
They're going to kick us off the ship.

488
00:33:31,985 --> 00:33:33,028
What?

489
00:33:33,612 --> 00:33:36,698
If I go, you, the girls, Tommy,
have a place to stay.

490
00:33:36,781 --> 00:33:39,618
If I don't, we're back in Philly tonight.

491
00:33:40,702 --> 00:33:43,121
What about Thierry?
Can't he do anything?

492
00:33:43,622 --> 00:33:46,708
Men like Thierry
aren't in charge of anything anymore.

493
00:33:47,459 --> 00:33:49,294
You keep this with you.

494
00:33:49,377 --> 00:33:50,378
I'll call in once a day.

495
00:33:50,462 --> 00:33:52,839
As long as I make that call,
everything's gonna be okay.

496
00:33:54,549 --> 00:33:56,176
I'm coming back.

497
00:33:56,551 --> 00:33:58,678
Okay?
We're going to make the best of it.

498
00:34:00,221 --> 00:34:01,556
As we do.

499
00:34:01,806 --> 00:34:03,224
Like we do.

500
00:34:13,902 --> 00:34:16,905
Okay, baby doll,
Daddy's got to go to work.

501
00:34:17,447 --> 00:34:19,115
I'm not a baby.

502
00:34:20,075 --> 00:34:21,242
Okay.

503
00:34:21,576 --> 00:34:23,745
Tall, beautiful, tiny adult.

504
00:34:25,080 --> 00:34:27,165
I'll be back soon.

505
00:34:27,332 --> 00:34:28,458
Yeah?

506
00:34:29,918 --> 00:34:31,795
All right, tough guy...

507
00:34:32,379 --> 00:34:33,463
Take care of the ladies for me?

508
00:34:33,546 --> 00:34:34,589
Yeah.

509
00:34:34,714 --> 00:34:35,840
Deal.

510
00:34:37,550 --> 00:34:39,094
You're awesome.

511
00:34:45,975 --> 00:34:48,103
Daddy's coming back.

512
00:35:15,630 --> 00:35:17,132
This way, sir.

513
00:36:00,341 --> 00:36:01,426
Look.

514
00:36:01,509 --> 00:36:02,719
We don't know what we're walking into.

515
00:36:02,844 --> 00:36:04,804
So we do what they say. Okay.

516
00:36:04,971 --> 00:36:07,474
If they move, we move.
If they stop, we stop.

517
00:36:07,557 --> 00:36:09,225
If things were to get crazy,

518
00:36:09,517 --> 00:36:10,810
just focus on their boots,

519
00:36:10,894 --> 00:36:12,437
focus on their voices,
and we'll be all right.

520
00:36:12,520 --> 00:36:14,939
- Mmm-hmm.
- These guys are hammers.

521
00:36:15,023 --> 00:36:16,775
And to hammers,
everything looks like nails.

522
00:36:16,858 --> 00:36:17,942
I heard that.

523
00:36:18,026 --> 00:36:19,527
You were meant to.

524
00:36:19,694 --> 00:36:21,654
So, you see something that's important,

525
00:36:21,738 --> 00:36:23,948
you Call it out and we'll make it happen.

526
00:36:24,407 --> 00:36:25,617
Okay.

527
00:36:27,327 --> 00:36:29,496
You think we're gonna find anything?

528
00:36:30,163 --> 00:36:31,247
Yeah.

529
00:36:31,831 --> 00:36:33,500
Yeah, we're gonna find something.

530
00:36:34,876 --> 00:36:37,879
Mother Nature is a serial killer.

531
00:36:39,005 --> 00:36:40,507
No one's better.

532
00:36:40,840 --> 00:36:42,342
More creative.

533
00:36:43,551 --> 00:36:44,803
But like all serial killers,

534
00:36:44,886 --> 00:36:47,680
she can't help the urge
to want to get caught.

535
00:36:48,348 --> 00:36:49,933
What good are all those brilliant crimes

536
00:36:50,016 --> 00:36:52,101
if no one takes the credit?

537
00:36:52,227 --> 00:36:54,187
So she leaves crumbs.

538
00:36:55,230 --> 00:36:57,273
Now, the hard part,
why you spend a decade in school,

539
00:36:57,398 --> 00:37:00,318
is seeing the crumbs
for the clues they are.

540
00:37:00,944 --> 00:37:03,029
Sometimes the thing you thought

541
00:37:03,238 --> 00:37:06,574
was the most brutal aspect of the virus,

542
00:37:07,408 --> 00:37:09,744
turns out to be the chink in its armor.

543
00:37:12,080 --> 00:37:15,750
And she loves disguising
her weaknesses as strengths.

544
00:37:18,253 --> 00:37:19,796
She's a bitch.

545
00:37:30,974 --> 00:37:33,393
Aftention.
D.C. has gone dark. I repeat,

546
00:37:33,476 --> 00:37:34,811
D.C. has gone dark.

547
00:37:34,936 --> 00:37:36,896
The Capitol evacuation
has been suspended.

548
00:37:37,313 --> 00:37:41,484
All available resources should be
directed to Naval Station Norfolk.

549
00:37:42,777 --> 00:37:44,904
All non-essential personne!

550
00:37:44,988 --> 00:37:47,699
given F-6 status
and in groups A through E

551
00:37:47,782 --> 00:37:50,618
need to report
to the flight deck for relocation.

552
00:37:51,953 --> 00:37:55,039
Groups A and B relocating to Orlando

553
00:37:55,123 --> 00:37:57,542
should be on the stern
clear of the landing zone.

554
00:37:59,627 --> 00:38:03,756
I say again, all non-essential
personnel given F-6 status

555
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:05,842
need to report to the flight deck.

556
00:38:06,009 --> 00:38:08,887
Choppers are inbound
for immediate relocation.

557
00:38:17,979 --> 00:38:19,814
Mommy, is this dinner?

558
00:38:20,148 --> 00:38:21,274
Yes, sweetheart.

559
00:38:21,357 --> 00:38:23,318
Water here tastes funny.

560
00:38:23,818 --> 00:38:25,445
It's jet fuel, young lady.

561
00:38:25,820 --> 00:38:27,238
He's joking.

562
00:38:28,323 --> 00:38:32,160
I wish. Desal has trouble filtering it out.

563
00:38:32,994 --> 00:38:36,372
Probably because
there's too many people on this ship.

564
00:38:46,674 --> 00:38:48,676
Everybody wake up.

565
00:38:49,385 --> 00:38:51,804
We're on approach
to Camp Humphreys.

566
00:38:51,888 --> 00:38:55,266
Most of the base is dark,
and no one is manning the tower.

567
00:38:55,350 --> 00:38:57,352
We're running on fumes,
so there's really no choice,

568
00:38:57,435 --> 00:38:58,811
I've got to put us down.

569
00:38:58,895 --> 00:39:00,229
So buckle up.

570
00:39:26,756 --> 00:39:27,882
Hold up.

571
00:39:28,591 --> 00:39:30,677
Keep your finger off the trigger.

572
00:39:37,558 --> 00:39:38,726
Okay.

573
00:40:05,086 --> 00:40:06,504
Fassbach! Wait!

574
00:40:09,090 --> 00:40:10,383
Damn it.

575
00:40:18,266 --> 00:40:19,267
Move back!

576
00:40:20,435 --> 00:40:23,229
Friendly! Friendly!
Keep it down. Keep it down.

577
00:40:23,312 --> 00:40:25,106
What is this? What happened to him?

578
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:26,649
He slipped. He's dead.

579
00:40:26,733 --> 00:40:28,693
Come on! Come on! Let's go! Let's go!

580
00:40:46,627 --> 00:40:47,795
Okay, I'm good!

581
00:40:48,087 --> 00:40:50,131
- Who was it? Who fell?
- Skilken.

582
00:40:50,298 --> 00:40:52,300
- Hold! Clear.
- Hold.

583
00:40:54,093 --> 00:40:55,762
I want an ammo count,
then you reload your mags!

584
00:40:55,845 --> 00:40:56,888
Yes, sir!

585
00:40:56,971 --> 00:40:58,890
My boy who just died out there was 23.

586
00:40:59,682 --> 00:41:01,017
He was 23.

587
00:41:01,601 --> 00:41:03,352
You want to tell me why?

588
00:41:03,436 --> 00:41:07,190
Because the guy who just shot
himself, he's a doctor, a virologist.

589
00:41:07,857 --> 00:41:08,983
What are you talking about?

590
00:41:09,067 --> 00:41:10,860
He was supposed
to be our best hope.

591
00:41:10,943 --> 00:41:12,570
Well, he's not our best hope anymore.

592
00:41:12,653 --> 00:41:14,781
Hey.
That guy volunteered to come here.

593
00:41:14,864 --> 00:41:16,282
He didn't have to, you know.

594
00:41:16,365 --> 00:41:17,617
None of them did.

595
00:41:17,825 --> 00:41:19,952
We're still trying to figure out
what the hell this thing is.

596
00:41:20,369 --> 00:41:22,789
Well, shit happens.

597
00:41:24,332 --> 00:41:26,501
The doctor would have
strongly agreed with you.

598
00:41:26,584 --> 00:41:28,044
How do we go about refueling?

599
00:41:28,127 --> 00:41:31,297
When I say so. And very carefully.

600
00:41:32,256 --> 00:41:34,592
The noise, are they drawn to it?

601
00:41:34,926 --> 00:41:37,386
Yeah. Sound draws them.

602
00:41:37,720 --> 00:41:40,139
Body shots only seem
to slow them down.

603
00:41:40,223 --> 00:41:42,683
Head shots do the trick,
but just to be safe

604
00:41:42,767 --> 00:41:44,852
we tend to burn them when we can.

605
00:41:45,186 --> 00:41:47,146
- You fought any Zeke yet?
- Yeah.

606
00:41:47,355 --> 00:41:49,690
- Where?
- Philly. Newark.

607
00:41:50,066 --> 00:41:51,109
Bad?

608
00:41:54,153 --> 00:41:55,363
- What about Houston?
- St. Louis?

609
00:41:55,530 --> 00:41:56,572
- Baltimore?
- Atlanta?

610
00:41:56,656 --> 00:41:57,824
Detroit?

611
00:41:57,990 --> 00:41:59,117
Guys, I'll be honest with you,

612
00:41:59,200 --> 00:42:02,203
I don't know of any place back
home that's doing very well.

613
00:42:02,286 --> 00:42:03,704
All right...

614
00:42:05,373 --> 00:42:08,292
If the other guy was a virologist,
what do you do?

615
00:42:08,376 --> 00:42:11,879
There was a memo
sent from this installation 11 days ago.

616
00:42:12,171 --> 00:42:13,422
It had the word "zombie" in it.

617
00:42:13,506 --> 00:42:15,466
Do you know anything about it?

618
00:42:15,550 --> 00:42:16,634
Yeah.

619
00:42:17,009 --> 00:42:19,428
It was an email, not a memo.

620
00:42:19,929 --> 00:42:22,390
Pretty obvious
nobody back home bothered to read it.

621
00:42:27,353 --> 00:42:30,523
Now, there's 15, 16 guys in this room.

622
00:42:30,857 --> 00:42:33,860
Most of them guards.
But all of them were bitten

623
00:42:33,943 --> 00:42:36,154
trying to get this man
handcuffed to the cot.

624
00:42:36,529 --> 00:42:39,574
Now, our colonel
said he was the first one.

625
00:42:39,991 --> 00:42:41,659
This colonel, is he around?

626
00:42:41,742 --> 00:42:42,952
Oh, yeah. He's right here.

627
00:42:50,418 --> 00:42:53,171
The guy who's shackled, do you know

628
00:42:53,421 --> 00:42:55,089
who bit him, what bit him?

629
00:42:55,423 --> 00:42:57,216
He was the base doctor.

630
00:42:59,218 --> 00:43:01,220
He'd just returned from the field.

631
00:43:01,554 --> 00:43:04,473
He'd been sent out
to verify the death of a soldier

632
00:43:04,557 --> 00:43:06,809
who had just gone AWOL
the week before.

633
00:43:07,226 --> 00:43:09,270
Some villagers had found this guy

634
00:43:09,353 --> 00:43:11,981
foaming at the mouth,
oozing some kind of black tar.

635
00:43:12,815 --> 00:43:14,901
Then he tried to bite one of them.

636
00:43:14,984 --> 00:43:17,278
They shot him, tied him up,
threw him in a barn.

637
00:43:31,417 --> 00:43:33,044
That's all we know, except the doctor

638
00:43:33,127 --> 00:43:36,214
comes back here
and begins attacking his patients.

639
00:43:36,297 --> 00:43:38,883
This soldier,
do you know where he came from?

640
00:43:39,133 --> 00:43:40,134
No.

641
00:43:40,218 --> 00:43:43,221
Anyone he might
have come in contact with?

642
00:43:43,304 --> 00:43:44,305
No.

643
00:43:44,388 --> 00:43:45,890
There's got to be records.

644
00:43:47,767 --> 00:43:49,644
You are welcome
to take a look if you want.

645
00:43:53,064 --> 00:43:55,650
Then the origin could
have come from anywhere.

646
00:43:55,983 --> 00:43:57,068
It's a shame you had to fly

647
00:43:57,151 --> 00:43:59,153
all the way out here to figure that out.

648
00:44:03,157 --> 00:44:04,825
How did you all escape this?

649
00:44:05,076 --> 00:44:07,411
The expenditure of ammunition.

650
00:44:08,913 --> 00:44:10,748
Is that how you tweaked your leg?

651
00:44:12,583 --> 00:44:14,460
No, shit's been bugging me a while.

652
00:44:15,503 --> 00:44:18,297
This prick stands right in the mix,

653
00:44:18,381 --> 00:44:19,757
while seven or eight of them

654
00:44:19,840 --> 00:44:21,676
turn Zeke all at the same time.

655
00:44:21,759 --> 00:44:23,803
But they got no time
for Ol' Dirty Bastard here.

656
00:44:23,886 --> 00:44:26,264
Biting everything like fat kids love Twix.

657
00:44:27,848 --> 00:44:29,433
Got no time for his lucky ass.

658
00:44:29,517 --> 00:44:31,185
Ain't it obvious I'm charmed?

659
00:44:31,519 --> 00:44:34,522
The ones I saw bitten
turned in 12 seconds. Same here?

660
00:44:34,689 --> 00:44:36,023
Five or 10 minutes.

661
00:44:36,190 --> 00:44:39,443
Yeah, Davidson went
and he turned in 10 minutes.

662
00:44:39,777 --> 00:44:40,945
"Stevie?

663
00:44:41,028 --> 00:44:44,365
"Captain Spekes! Oh, my God!
My God! My God! Are they eating me?"

664
00:44:45,032 --> 00:44:46,033
Who's that?

665
00:44:46,158 --> 00:44:47,827
Waste no time on that freak.

666
00:44:48,202 --> 00:44:49,287
He's C.I.A.

667
00:44:49,370 --> 00:44:51,289
Got caught selling guns to North Korea.

668
00:44:51,372 --> 00:44:52,707
Davidson,

669
00:44:53,207 --> 00:44:55,376
he turned in 10 minutes.

670
00:44:55,710 --> 00:44:59,046
That doesn't sound viral
to me at all, sports fans!

671
00:45:02,008 --> 00:45:03,801
You're with the C.1.A.?

672
00:45:07,471 --> 00:45:08,806
But they're not with me.

673
00:45:13,060 --> 00:45:14,603
And who are you?

674
00:45:14,687 --> 00:45:16,105
U.N.

675
00:45:16,188 --> 00:45:17,857
Oh, my God!

676
00:45:20,484 --> 00:45:22,528
Captain, put on the World Music!

677
00:45:22,862 --> 00:45:24,530
The day

678
00:45:25,323 --> 00:45:26,991
is saved!

679
00:45:27,742 --> 00:45:28,909
Why'd you sell guns to the North?

680
00:45:28,993 --> 00:45:30,077
Why not?

681
00:45:30,244 --> 00:45:31,495
Are they surviving this?

682
00:45:31,579 --> 00:45:32,788
Indeed they are.

683
00:45:32,872 --> 00:45:34,332
Using your guns.

684
00:45:34,415 --> 00:45:37,418
Guns are half-measures.

685
00:45:37,710 --> 00:45:38,753
How then?

686
00:45:42,173 --> 00:45:43,299
All right.

687
00:46:08,866 --> 00:46:10,368
They took away

688
00:46:11,660 --> 00:46:15,373
the Zekes' exponential power.

689
00:46:17,041 --> 00:46:20,544
They pulled the teeth of all 23 million

690
00:46:20,961 --> 00:46:24,215
in less than 24 hours.

691
00:46:28,636 --> 00:46:31,680
The greatest feat
of social engineering in history.

692
00:46:32,139 --> 00:46:33,641
It's brilliant.

693
00:46:34,016 --> 00:46:35,309
No teeth,

694
00:46:36,352 --> 00:46:37,645
no bite.

695
00:46:38,270 --> 00:46:39,855
No great spread.

696
00:46:43,901 --> 00:46:44,985
Bullshit.

697
00:46:45,194 --> 00:46:48,614
More books,
fewer receptions, Boutros Boutros.

698
00:46:49,031 --> 00:46:50,991
Now, why do you have to burn them

699
00:46:51,075 --> 00:46:52,827
to ashes to get them to finally stop?

700
00:46:52,910 --> 00:46:54,495
Why do they move like a plague?

701
00:46:54,578 --> 00:46:56,288
Why is Israel winning?

702
00:46:57,373 --> 00:46:58,958
How is Israel winning?

703
00:46:59,750 --> 00:47:02,002
They sealed off their entire country

704
00:47:02,711 --> 00:47:05,673
days before the undead attacked man.

705
00:47:06,132 --> 00:47:07,466
First to know,

706
00:47:08,008 --> 00:47:09,468
first to act.

707
00:47:09,760 --> 00:47:11,887
People have been
building walls there for two millennia.

708
00:47:12,012 --> 00:47:14,682
Mmm. Right. Yeah, but,

709
00:47:14,765 --> 00:47:16,475
finish all those

710
00:47:16,559 --> 00:47:19,186
thousands of years of work a week ago?

711
00:47:20,104 --> 00:47:21,564
Impeccable timing is all.

712
00:47:25,192 --> 00:47:26,861
You want answers?

713
00:47:28,821 --> 00:47:30,531
Jurgen Warmbrunn.

714
00:47:31,574 --> 00:47:35,578
That's the man
in Jerusalem you want to see.

715
00:47:36,912 --> 00:47:38,080
You ever seen anything like that?

716
00:47:38,205 --> 00:47:39,373
Hell, no.

717
00:47:39,457 --> 00:47:42,793
We're going to Jerusalem.
I'm your co-pilot.

718
00:47:49,425 --> 00:47:50,551
Oh, hang on.

719
00:47:50,759 --> 00:47:52,386
Hang on. Hang on a minute.

720
00:47:53,429 --> 00:47:54,680
Hello?

721
00:47:56,265 --> 00:47:57,475
Gerry?

722
00:47:58,392 --> 00:48:00,311
- Honey?
- Gerry, can you hear me?

723
00:48:00,394 --> 00:48:01,437
Karin?

724
00:48:02,188 --> 00:48:03,439
Hello?

725
00:48:06,567 --> 00:48:08,235
God damn it!

726
00:48:17,953 --> 00:48:19,622
Give me your hand.

727
00:48:22,625 --> 00:48:23,667
No way. No.

728
00:48:23,751 --> 00:48:25,002
My mother. Dallas.

729
00:48:25,085 --> 00:48:27,671
Probably pacing a hole
in the floor right now if she's still there.

730
00:48:27,755 --> 00:48:30,299
Better chance of you seeing
her before me, that's all.

731
00:48:30,382 --> 00:48:32,843
It's a big plane. We got a lot of room.

732
00:48:32,927 --> 00:48:35,930
Better the devil you know
than the one you don't.

733
00:48:36,388 --> 00:48:39,058
You'll be all right.
Just pedal your ass off.

734
00:48:39,266 --> 00:48:41,352
Make sure Maverick here keeps
the nose of that plane

735
00:48:41,435 --> 00:48:42,520
pointed towards the sun.

736
00:48:42,603 --> 00:48:45,856
Just remember, don't lock
the bowser's fuel line to the inlet.

737
00:48:45,940 --> 00:48:47,441
Tell me 10 more times.

738
00:48:47,525 --> 00:48:48,984
- You good?
- Right here.

739
00:48:49,068 --> 00:48:51,111
All right. Don't rush.

740
00:48:51,820 --> 00:48:54,490
We've got one chance
to fuel their plane, so let's do it right.

741
00:48:54,740 --> 00:48:56,742
If you ain't a crack shot,
don't aim for the head,

742
00:48:56,825 --> 00:48:57,868
just get Zeke on the ground.

743
00:48:57,952 --> 00:49:01,080
Remember, "Spine's divine,
those knees they work just fine!"

744
00:49:01,163 --> 00:49:02,957
Let's go, lights out!

745
00:49:23,352 --> 00:49:25,604
Alpha in position.

746
00:49:25,688 --> 00:49:27,731
Bravo moving out.

747
00:49:27,815 --> 00:49:30,234
Remember, these things
are drawn to sound.

748
00:49:30,317 --> 00:49:33,404
So I need you close to target
before I bring you the truck.

749
00:49:33,487 --> 00:49:36,198
Now there's only one way
we're getting you on that plane,

750
00:49:36,282 --> 00:49:38,325
and that's quietly.

751
00:50:07,938 --> 00:50:08,981
Shit!

752
00:50:09,064 --> 00:50:10,858
God damn it!
Shut that thing off!

753
00:50:15,446 --> 00:50:16,822
Looks like we just woke the dead.

754
00:50:18,032 --> 00:50:19,116
Out of respect for others,

755
00:50:19,199 --> 00:50:20,909
please turn off all pagers
and cell phones.

756
00:50:24,038 --> 00:50:25,581
We got to move.

757
00:50:26,290 --> 00:50:28,208
We've got to get out of here, let's move!

758
00:50:34,757 --> 00:50:35,966
Go, go, go!

759
00:50:41,889 --> 00:50:43,098
Whoo!

760
00:50:45,934 --> 00:50:47,186
I'm gonna clear a path through Zeke!

761
00:50:47,269 --> 00:50:48,729
You pedal like hell!

762
00:50:51,273 --> 00:50:53,734
Come on, boys,
I need head shots! Tap 'em out!

763
00:50:53,817 --> 00:50:55,527
I want to see some Zeke on the ground!

764
00:51:33,482 --> 00:51:36,151
You're kidding me.
I'm a God damn Zeke.

765
00:51:37,486 --> 00:51:39,947
I got you, Captain. Just say the word.

766
00:51:40,656 --> 00:51:43,450
It's all right, boys. I got this one.

767
00:51:45,828 --> 00:51:47,454
- God damn it.
- We got enough!

768
00:51:48,038 --> 00:51:49,957
We need to detach the fuel line!

769
00:51:51,667 --> 00:51:53,669
Israel better pay off.

770
00:52:03,637 --> 00:52:05,431
All right, I have instrument,
but only on single prop.

771
00:52:05,514 --> 00:52:06,640
You'll have to talk me through it.

772
00:52:09,810 --> 00:52:11,061
Okay, we're clear.

773
00:52:11,145 --> 00:52:12,563
Okay. Give me all the lights.

774
00:52:15,315 --> 00:52:16,942
Switch on the anti-icing.

775
00:52:17,025 --> 00:52:18,026
- Where?
- The red knob.

776
00:52:18,152 --> 00:52:20,529
- Got it, got it.
- Set up our heading 020 for departure.

777
00:52:21,029 --> 00:52:23,323
- We got to move!
- Set flaps 15 degrees.

778
00:52:23,490 --> 00:52:24,825
Flaps 15.

779
00:52:24,992 --> 00:52:27,327
All right, we are all set.
Let's get out of here!

780
00:52:29,872 --> 00:52:31,206
Make it steep.

781
00:52:51,351 --> 00:52:52,686
- Gerry?
- Hi, baby.

782
00:52:52,770 --> 00:52:53,854
Hi. Hi.

783
00:52:55,731 --> 00:52:57,566
I tried to call you.

784
00:52:58,400 --> 00:53:00,235
I know, I was...

785
00:53:00,778 --> 00:53:02,988
It was bad timing, I was running around.

786
00:53:03,530 --> 00:53:05,032
Are you okay?

787
00:53:09,495 --> 00:53:11,997
Yeah, everything's okay. I'm okay.

788
00:53:13,665 --> 00:53:15,167
That's the spirit.

789
00:53:15,709 --> 00:53:16,835
Yeah.

790
00:53:17,461 --> 00:53:18,754
Listen,

791
00:53:19,087 --> 00:53:20,756
Korea didn't work out.

792
00:53:23,884 --> 00:53:26,428
Now it looks like
we're gonna have to go to Israel.

793
00:53:26,512 --> 00:53:28,639
Try to get some rest on the flight.

794
00:53:29,473 --> 00:53:31,058
How are the kids?

795
00:53:31,683 --> 00:53:32,684
Um...

796
00:53:34,561 --> 00:53:35,896
I think...

797
00:53:37,564 --> 00:53:40,067
They're really... They're good.

798
00:53:41,235 --> 00:53:43,070
I got Connie right here.

799
00:53:54,081 --> 00:53:55,249
Baby?

800
00:54:12,266 --> 00:54:14,852
Attention, unidentified aircraft.

801
00:54:14,935 --> 00:54:18,188
You are in a restricted airspace
and not clear for landing.

802
00:54:18,605 --> 00:54:20,774
Jerusalem tower, Reach 394.

803
00:54:21,024 --> 00:54:22,985
Pan, pan, pan.
Request immediate landing.

804
00:54:23,068 --> 00:54:25,571
Contact Mossad,
office of Jurgen Warmbrunn.

805
00:54:25,654 --> 00:54:27,281
Special Envoy, United Nations.

806
00:54:37,457 --> 00:54:41,169
Stay with the plane. Be ready to bug out.
I'll be back before dark.

807
00:55:36,808 --> 00:55:38,143
The problem
with most people is that

808
00:55:38,226 --> 00:55:39,895
they don't believe
something can happen

809
00:55:40,187 --> 00:55:42,022
until it already has.

810
00:55:42,272 --> 00:55:44,191
It's not stupidity or weakness.

811
00:55:45,400 --> 00:55:47,110
It's just human nature.

812
00:55:50,113 --> 00:55:51,448
How did you know?

813
00:55:51,698 --> 00:55:53,200
Gerald Lane.

814
00:55:53,784 --> 00:55:56,244
Wrote a self-defeating Jeremiad

815
00:55:56,328 --> 00:55:59,498
about his employer,
the U.N., back in 2010.

816
00:56:00,374 --> 00:56:03,335
Caused a few ripples.
Sidelined your career.

817
00:56:04,336 --> 00:56:07,130
Thought you'd have parlayed
those ripples into a self-righteous book.

818
00:56:07,214 --> 00:56:08,882
No nose for profit.

819
00:56:09,299 --> 00:56:11,134
How did Israel know?

820
00:56:11,927 --> 00:56:15,055
We intercepted a communique
from an Indian general

821
00:56:15,472 --> 00:56:17,975
saying they were
fighting the Rakshasha.

822
00:56:18,058 --> 00:56:20,644
Translation, zombies.

823
00:56:21,061 --> 00:56:23,313
Technically undead.

824
00:56:26,066 --> 00:56:27,484
Jurgen Warmbrunn.

825
00:56:27,567 --> 00:56:29,987
High-ranking official in the Mossad.

826
00:56:30,320 --> 00:56:35,075
Described as sober, efficient,
not terribly imaginative.

827
00:56:35,575 --> 00:56:38,704
And yet you build a wall
because you read a communique

828
00:56:38,787 --> 00:56:40,956
that mentions the word "zombie"?

829
00:56:42,124 --> 00:56:45,794
Well, when put like that,
I'd be skeptical as well.

830
00:56:46,628 --> 00:56:48,672
In the '30s, Jews refused to believe

831
00:56:48,755 --> 00:56:51,258
they could be sent
to concentration camps.

832
00:56:51,550 --> 00:56:55,762
In '72, we refused to fathom
we'd be massacred in the Olympics.

833
00:56:56,263 --> 00:57:00,392
In the month before October 1973,
we saw Arab troop movements,

834
00:57:00,475 --> 00:57:03,228
and we unanimously agreed
they didn't pose a threat.

835
00:57:04,021 --> 00:57:08,400
Well, a month later, the Arab attack
almost drove us into the sea.

836
00:57:09,067 --> 00:57:11,445
So we decided to make a change.

837
00:57:12,487 --> 00:57:13,739
A change?

838
00:57:14,239 --> 00:57:15,574
The Tenth Man.

839
00:57:16,950 --> 00:57:18,910
If nine of us
look at the same information

840
00:57:18,994 --> 00:57:21,538
and arrive at the exact same conclusion,

841
00:57:21,621 --> 00:57:24,291
it's the duty of the tenth man
to disagree.

842
00:57:24,750 --> 00:57:27,169
No matter how improbable it may seem,

843
00:57:27,252 --> 00:57:29,296
the tenth man has to start digging

844
00:57:29,379 --> 00:57:31,673
on the assumption
that the other nine are wrong.

845
00:57:33,800 --> 00:57:35,302
And you were that tenth man.

846
00:57:36,219 --> 00:57:37,262
Precisely.

847
00:57:43,643 --> 00:57:48,023
Since everyone assumed that this talk of
zombies was cover for something else,

848
00:57:48,106 --> 00:57:51,193
I began my investigation
on the assumption

849
00:57:51,276 --> 00:57:55,489
that when they said "zombies,"
they meant zombies.

850
00:57:56,656 --> 00:57:58,200
Was patient zero from India?

851
00:57:58,492 --> 00:57:59,785
That's the problem.

852
00:57:59,868 --> 00:58:01,411
There's so many
potential sources in play

853
00:58:01,495 --> 00:58:03,288
that no one knows where it began.

854
00:58:04,247 --> 00:58:06,166
The organ trade in Germany.

855
00:58:06,666 --> 00:58:10,378
Strange examples of violent behavior
across the Asian peninsulas.

856
00:58:11,338 --> 00:58:15,008
Meanwhile, the zombie plague keeps
spreading, and we do what we can.

857
00:58:16,927 --> 00:58:19,179
These are
the Jerusalem Salvation Gates.

858
00:58:20,263 --> 00:58:21,765
Two of 10 portals

859
00:58:21,848 --> 00:58:24,643
through the security perimeter
into fortified Israel.

860
00:58:29,231 --> 00:58:31,024
You're letting people in.

861
00:58:31,441 --> 00:58:34,528
Every human being we save
is one less zombie to fight.

862
00:59:16,736 --> 00:59:18,071
It's okay.

863
00:59:44,931 --> 00:59:48,602
If I could get into India, where
would I start? Who would I speak with?

864
00:59:48,685 --> 00:59:50,604
India's a black hole.

865
00:59:50,687 --> 00:59:52,689
Forget about patient zero.

866
00:59:52,772 --> 00:59:55,317
I can't do that.
It's too late for me to build a wall.

867
00:59:59,905 --> 01:00:02,032
I'm running out of time. I need specifics.

868
01:00:02,115 --> 01:00:04,242
- I need answers...
- I don't have answers.

869
01:00:04,326 --> 01:00:06,453
All you can do is find a way to hide.

870
01:00:12,751 --> 01:00:14,294
Get troops down there.

871
01:00:27,349 --> 01:00:28,850
It's too loud! It's too loud!

872
01:00:33,313 --> 01:00:34,773
They're coming over the top!

873
01:00:45,951 --> 01:00:47,994
Shit!

874
01:00:48,245 --> 01:00:50,080
Command, we have a breach
at Salvation Gate.

875
01:00:50,163 --> 01:00:51,748
They're coming over the wall!

876
01:01:33,623 --> 01:01:36,376
Get him to Jaffa Gate.

877
01:01:54,728 --> 01:01:57,063
She'll get you out of here,
she'll get you to your plane!

878
01:02:22,047 --> 01:02:23,715
Stay low!

879
01:02:23,798 --> 01:02:25,342
Wrong way! Wrong way!

880
01:02:26,634 --> 01:02:29,763
Go to landing point B.

881
01:02:30,472 --> 01:02:32,974
Roger, we are inbound
to landing point B.

882
01:03:38,665 --> 01:03:40,834
Hawk 5, almost there.
E.T.A. one minute.

883
01:03:42,127 --> 01:03:44,754
Hawk 5. Hawk 5,
you're patched in. Over.

884
01:03:44,838 --> 01:03:46,881
This is Hawk 5. Listen carefully.

885
01:03:47,424 --> 01:03:50,718
The city is breached,
and they're heading towards the airport.

886
01:06:04,018 --> 01:06:05,270
One thousand one.

887
01:06:05,353 --> 01:06:06,646
One thousand two.

888
01:06:06,729 --> 01:06:09,023
One thousand three. One thousand four.

889
01:06:10,692 --> 01:06:12,110
One thousand five.

890
01:06:12,986 --> 01:06:14,279
One thousand six.

891
01:06:14,904 --> 01:06:16,322
One thousand seven.

892
01:06:17,699 --> 01:06:19,033
One thousand eight.

893
01:06:23,121 --> 01:06:24,247
We got to move.

894
01:06:35,341 --> 01:06:36,551
You'll be all right.

895
01:06:37,218 --> 01:06:39,512
You're not gonna turn.
You're not gonna turn!

896
01:06:42,056 --> 01:06:43,391
We got to move.

897
01:06:43,558 --> 01:06:45,310
We got to move!

898
01:07:10,877 --> 01:07:12,378
5 going down.

899
01:07:19,677 --> 01:07:20,803
Chopper 5 is down.

900
01:07:20,887 --> 01:07:22,472
I say again, chopper 5 is down.

901
01:07:22,555 --> 01:07:24,349
L.Z. iS overrun.

902
01:07:25,058 --> 01:07:28,936
Tower, Reach 394.
Requesting immediate departure.

903
01:07:29,228 --> 01:07:31,314
Tower to 394.
Proceed to runway four.

904
01:07:31,397 --> 01:07:32,649
Good luck out there.

905
01:07:49,832 --> 01:07:51,000
No!

906
01:07:54,379 --> 01:07:56,255
There! That one!

907
01:08:03,429 --> 01:08:04,847
Stop. Stop.

908
01:08:24,492 --> 01:08:25,660
Go! Go!

909
01:08:38,798 --> 01:08:40,133
Get them out of here!

910
01:08:45,012 --> 01:08:47,849
Stay calm, please.
Stay calm.

911
01:08:57,942 --> 01:08:59,902
Come on. Go, go, go.

912
01:09:06,826 --> 01:09:07,910
What's your destination?

913
01:09:07,994 --> 01:09:10,037
I don't know. We were headed here,
but I don't know.

914
01:11:17,582 --> 01:11:19,292
I'm Gerry, by the way.

915
01:11:20,585 --> 01:11:21,669
Segen.

916
01:11:22,670 --> 01:11:23,796
Segen.

917
01:11:24,797 --> 01:11:26,007
First or last?

918
01:11:27,174 --> 01:11:28,509
Just Segen.

919
01:11:28,885 --> 01:11:29,886
So, what we're doing,

920
01:11:29,969 --> 01:11:31,721
we've got to change this bandage
and we're gonna clean it.

921
01:11:31,804 --> 01:11:32,930
Okay?

922
01:11:37,143 --> 01:11:39,061
You okay? Okay?

923
01:11:43,316 --> 01:11:44,442
Okay.

924
01:11:47,612 --> 01:11:49,405
Come on, gut up. Gut up.

925
01:11:50,907 --> 01:11:52,199
Here we go.

926
01:11:54,160 --> 01:11:55,328
We're almost there.

927
01:11:56,495 --> 01:11:58,497
Okay. Big breaths.

928
01:11:58,998 --> 01:12:01,584
Let's get this over fast. Big breaths.

929
01:12:02,501 --> 01:12:03,669
Here we go.

930
01:12:08,049 --> 01:12:10,176
Come on. Good.

931
01:12:11,260 --> 01:12:13,179
Last step. Last step.

932
01:12:13,846 --> 01:12:14,889
Big breath.

933
01:12:16,766 --> 01:12:19,894
Good job. There it is. Okay.
Mmm-hmm.

934
01:12:23,105 --> 01:12:25,816
Okay. Okay, I think you've earned this.

935
01:12:29,445 --> 01:12:30,947
Very good. Okay.

936
01:12:32,114 --> 01:12:33,449
You a doctor?

937
01:12:33,950 --> 01:12:35,034
No.

938
01:12:35,451 --> 01:12:37,078
I've had some training in the field.

939
01:12:38,120 --> 01:12:40,122
How did you know?

940
01:12:41,123 --> 01:12:43,376
Cutting it off...
How did you know it would work?

941
01:12:43,751 --> 01:12:45,086
I didn't.

942
01:12:49,006 --> 01:12:51,550
Now I'm just a liability.

943
01:12:54,303 --> 01:12:55,721
This prick

944
01:12:55,805 --> 01:12:58,182
stands right in the mix,

945
01:12:58,265 --> 01:12:59,475
while seven or eight of them

946
01:12:59,558 --> 01:13:01,727
turn Zeke all at the same time.

947
01:13:01,811 --> 01:13:03,688
Is that how
you tweaked your leg?

948
01:13:04,772 --> 01:13:06,774
No, shit's been bugging me a while.

949
01:13:07,608 --> 01:13:09,777
Got no time for his lucky ass.

950
01:13:10,987 --> 01:13:13,614
Now, the hard part
is seeing the crumbs

951
01:13:13,698 --> 01:13:15,324
for the clues they are.

952
01:13:17,535 --> 01:13:19,453
And sometimes the thing you thought

953
01:13:19,662 --> 01:13:22,957
was the most brutal aspect of the virus

954
01:13:24,208 --> 01:13:26,711
turns out to be the chink in its armor.

955
01:13:27,003 --> 01:13:28,295
I don't have answers.

956
01:13:31,090 --> 01:13:34,093
All you can do is find a way to hide.

957
01:13:51,527 --> 01:13:52,611
Gerry?

958
01:13:52,695 --> 01:13:54,071
Are you okay? Where are you, baby?
What's happening?

959
01:13:54,155 --> 01:13:55,239
I love you. I'm sorry.

960
01:13:55,322 --> 01:13:56,490
But you've got to get Thierry now.

961
01:13:56,574 --> 01:13:57,616
I'll find him.

962
01:14:00,745 --> 01:14:02,705
- Thierry! Thierry.
- Excuse me. Karin.

963
01:14:02,788 --> 01:14:04,123
Gerry needs you. I love you.

964
01:14:05,458 --> 01:14:06,792
Gerry? Where are you?

965
01:14:07,209 --> 01:14:08,377
On the last flight out.

966
01:14:08,461 --> 01:14:10,504
Listen, my phone is dying
and I need some quick intel.

967
01:14:10,588 --> 01:14:12,673
You gotta locate the closest
medical research facility.

968
01:14:12,757 --> 01:14:15,551
A C.D.C., a W.H.O.,
something that makes vaccines.

969
01:14:15,634 --> 01:14:17,678
- And the closest airport to it.
- I don't understand.

970
01:14:18,262 --> 01:14:19,555
No time to explain.

971
01:14:19,638 --> 01:14:20,681
Just make it happen, man.

972
01:14:20,765 --> 01:14:21,932
Okay, Okay.

973
01:14:22,183 --> 01:14:24,977
But, Gerry,
I still don't know where you are.

974
01:14:31,150 --> 01:14:32,359
Well, go and find out what he needs.

975
01:14:34,236 --> 01:14:35,738
You're gonna want to take this.

976
01:14:37,531 --> 01:14:38,657
Take it.

977
01:14:50,628 --> 01:14:52,004
Your battery is dead.

978
01:14:53,547 --> 01:14:56,217
We made contact
with Cardiff Airport, Wales.

979
01:14:56,300 --> 01:14:58,469
Your people directed us.

980
01:14:58,552 --> 01:15:01,263
There is W.H.O.
research facility nearby,

981
01:15:01,347 --> 01:15:03,933
but they are not sure
it's still operational.

982
01:15:04,016 --> 01:15:05,226
This is location.

983
01:15:05,684 --> 01:15:07,019
Can we make it?

984
01:15:16,070 --> 01:15:18,197
Ladies and gentlemen,
this is your Captain.

985
01:15:18,280 --> 01:15:20,699
I'm glad to report that
we are on our final approach

986
01:15:20,783 --> 01:15:22,409
to Cardiff Airport in Wales.

987
01:15:22,493 --> 01:15:25,204
All European airports
are under lockdown.

988
01:15:25,287 --> 01:15:29,375
But we have been given
priority status and cleared for landing.

989
01:15:29,458 --> 01:15:32,128
We will be allowed to disembark.

990
01:15:33,045 --> 01:15:35,422
We are very, very lucky.

991
01:16:00,322 --> 01:16:02,324
Hey. Who do you belong to?

992
01:17:06,430 --> 01:17:07,514
What's there?

993
01:17:07,598 --> 01:17:08,641
What is it?

994
01:17:12,686 --> 01:17:14,897
You... Bags.

995
01:17:16,273 --> 01:17:17,983
We need trolley and bags.

996
01:19:22,900 --> 01:19:25,235
Mayday, mayday, mayday!
Bravo 160 heavy.

997
01:19:25,319 --> 01:19:26,820
Emergency descent!

998
01:20:18,622 --> 01:20:19,832
Prepare for impact.

999
01:22:35,968 --> 01:22:37,302
Got to move.

1000
01:23:44,369 --> 01:23:45,704
Come on, come on.

1001
01:24:07,017 --> 01:24:08,352
Give me something good.

1002
01:24:08,435 --> 01:24:10,812
Sir, Cardiff Airport
lost contact with the plane.

1003
01:24:10,896 --> 01:24:13,190
Lane is M.LA. I'm sorry, sir.

1004
01:24:28,205 --> 01:24:30,707
Chopper inbound
for immediate relocation.

1005
01:24:30,791 --> 01:24:32,000
I say again.

1006
01:24:32,084 --> 01:24:34,670
All non-essential personnel
given F-6 status

1007
01:24:34,753 --> 01:24:37,297
need to report for immediate relocation.

1008
01:24:39,424 --> 01:24:40,676
Ma'am?

1009
01:24:41,051 --> 01:24:42,928
Thierry would like a word with you.

1010
01:24:49,434 --> 01:24:51,353
Captain, it's only been 48 hours.

1011
01:24:51,436 --> 01:24:54,940
He's a resourceful man. There's every
chance he could have survived.

1012
01:24:55,023 --> 01:24:58,110
Sir, I gave him my word
we would look after his family.

1013
01:24:58,652 --> 01:25:00,153
Yes, sir. I understand.

1014
01:25:04,366 --> 01:25:07,661
Okay. Let's go. We're good.

1015
01:25:54,291 --> 01:25:55,542
Daddy!

1016
01:26:06,762 --> 01:26:08,346
Daddy!

1017
01:26:08,764 --> 01:26:09,765
Daddy!

1018
01:27:16,081 --> 01:27:18,166
You're a tough bastard.

1019
01:27:18,250 --> 01:27:19,584
And a lucky one.

1020
01:27:20,252 --> 01:27:21,753
Who are you?

1021
01:27:23,630 --> 01:27:26,716
I came here with a... With a woman.

1022
01:27:26,800 --> 01:27:29,094
Is she still...

1023
01:27:29,886 --> 01:27:33,265
Who are you?
Why have you come here?

1024
01:27:38,019 --> 01:27:39,396
Why do you keep looking at him?

1025
01:27:40,772 --> 01:27:42,858
'Cause he's the one in charge.

1026
01:27:47,112 --> 01:27:48,530
You know what this place is?

1027
01:27:49,072 --> 01:27:50,866
Of course I do. That's why I'm here.

1028
01:27:50,949 --> 01:27:53,451
Then you understand
how this must look to us.

1029
01:27:55,036 --> 01:27:56,121
This

1030
01:27:56,705 --> 01:27:58,540
is important to you?

1031
01:27:59,583 --> 01:28:01,835
- How long have I been out?
- Three days.

1032
01:28:02,085 --> 01:28:03,295
Give me the phone.

1033
01:28:03,503 --> 01:28:04,838
Just give me the phone.

1034
01:28:05,088 --> 01:28:07,215
Give me the God damn phone!
Give me the phone!

1035
01:28:07,299 --> 01:28:09,134
As soon as you answer my question.

1036
01:28:10,969 --> 01:28:12,137
Call it.

1037
01:28:13,138 --> 01:28:15,473
Call the number,
they'll tell you who I am. Call it.

1038
01:28:26,651 --> 01:28:27,694
Gerry?

1039
01:28:28,153 --> 01:28:30,322
- Yeah, I'm here. I'm here.
- My God.

1040
01:28:30,947 --> 01:28:32,449
We thought you were dead.

1041
01:28:32,616 --> 01:28:33,950
Gerry, where are you?

1042
01:28:34,284 --> 01:28:36,328
Thierry, I'm with
a couple of nervous gentlemen.

1043
01:28:36,411 --> 01:28:37,996
They need some bona fides
before I can speak with you.

1044
01:28:38,079 --> 01:28:39,122
Of course.

1045
01:28:39,748 --> 01:28:41,374
This is Thierry Umutoni.

1046
01:28:42,125 --> 01:28:44,294
Deputy Secretary-General.
United Nations.

1047
01:28:44,669 --> 01:28:46,338
To whom am I speaking?

1048
01:28:46,671 --> 01:28:47,756
Where's Karin?

1049
01:28:48,924 --> 01:28:50,926
Thierry, why didn't Karin answer?

1050
01:28:56,181 --> 01:28:57,349
I'm sorry, Gerry.

1051
01:28:57,766 --> 01:28:59,100
I did what I could.

1052
01:29:01,561 --> 01:29:02,854
What does that mean?

1053
01:29:02,938 --> 01:29:04,648
You've got to calm down.
No, stop! Stop.

1054
01:29:04,731 --> 01:29:06,399
You're going to hurt yourself.

1055
01:29:25,210 --> 01:29:26,211
You're okay.

1056
01:29:28,672 --> 01:29:31,675
His family has been sent
to a refugee camp in Nova Scotia.

1057
01:29:32,634 --> 01:29:34,386
I'm sure they'll be safe.

1058
01:29:34,678 --> 01:29:38,598
Are you? Thierry told you
who I am and what I used to do, right?

1059
01:29:38,723 --> 01:29:39,724
Yeah.

1060
01:29:39,808 --> 01:29:42,060
Then trust me when
I tell you they're not safe.

1061
01:29:44,854 --> 01:29:46,189
I understand how you feel.

1062
01:29:46,523 --> 01:29:47,983
- Do you? Yes?
- Yes.

1063
01:29:48,400 --> 01:29:49,901
Do you have a family?

1064
01:29:50,986 --> 01:29:52,320
- No.
- No.

1065
01:29:52,696 --> 01:29:55,407
Then you couldn't possibly understand,
could you?

1066
01:29:56,199 --> 01:29:58,535
I lost my son and wife in Rome.

1067
01:30:00,537 --> 01:30:03,039
Rather, I lost my son to

1068
01:30:04,749 --> 01:30:07,585
something that had once been my wife.

1069
01:30:10,922 --> 01:30:13,258
We have all lost someone, Mr. Lane.

1070
01:30:14,384 --> 01:30:16,511
In your case, there is hope at least.

1071
01:30:16,594 --> 01:30:17,887
I'm sorry.

1072
01:30:19,764 --> 01:30:20,890
I'm sorry.

1073
01:30:20,974 --> 01:30:22,308
Now,

1074
01:30:23,393 --> 01:30:25,103
why did you come here?

1075
01:30:26,104 --> 01:30:28,189
What do you need from us?

1076
01:30:28,982 --> 01:30:30,567
Your worst disease.

1077
01:30:34,863 --> 01:30:36,197
He wants a what?

1078
01:30:36,281 --> 01:30:37,782
Deadly pathogen.

1079
01:30:38,283 --> 01:30:40,076
With a high mortality rate.

1080
01:30:40,785 --> 01:30:43,204
- But curable.
- Okay, well...

1081
01:30:43,288 --> 01:30:45,665
You'd want a bacteria
rather than a virus,

1082
01:30:45,749 --> 01:30:47,000
I would think. Typhus?

1083
01:30:47,792 --> 01:30:49,294
Meningitis. Scarlet Fever.

1084
01:30:49,377 --> 01:30:50,545
Rocky Mountain Fever.

1085
01:30:51,129 --> 01:30:53,465
Anyway, excuse me, what's this for?

1086
01:30:53,757 --> 01:30:57,594
Mr. Lane believes we can use
such a disease against the undead.

1087
01:30:57,802 --> 01:31:01,306
I would give you points
for originality, Mr. Lane,

1088
01:31:01,389 --> 01:31:03,308
if we hadn't already tried that, first thing.

1089
01:31:03,433 --> 01:31:09,147
One of the many things a virus or
bacteria needs to thrive is a live host.

1090
01:31:09,272 --> 01:31:10,690
A functioning circulatory system.

1091
01:31:10,815 --> 01:31:12,942
I'm afraid it boils down
to one simple fact...

1092
01:31:13,026 --> 01:31:14,694
You can't make a dead person sick.

1093
01:31:16,196 --> 01:31:17,697
It's not for them.

1094
01:31:18,448 --> 01:31:19,949
It's for us.

1095
01:31:21,659 --> 01:31:24,079
I believe these things have a weakness.

1096
01:31:24,788 --> 01:31:26,706
And that weakness is weakness.

1097
01:31:27,207 --> 01:31:28,875
Our weakness.

1098
01:31:28,958 --> 01:31:31,336
I have witnessed them
literally bypass people.

1099
01:31:31,503 --> 01:31:34,172
Walk right around them like
a river around a rock. Why?

1100
01:31:35,006 --> 01:31:37,300
I think, because those people were sick.

1101
01:31:37,842 --> 01:31:39,177
I think they were terminal.

1102
01:31:39,260 --> 01:31:40,678
And these things could sense it.

1103
01:31:41,012 --> 01:31:43,098
I think they're spreading a pathogen,

1104
01:31:43,181 --> 01:31:44,891
and they need a healthy host.

1105
01:31:45,141 --> 01:31:47,268
But even if you're right, I mean,
infecting the populace

1106
01:31:47,352 --> 01:31:49,521
with a lethal illness is not exactly a cure.

1107
01:31:50,021 --> 01:31:52,482
It's not a cure. It's camouflage.

1108
01:31:56,111 --> 01:31:57,445
It's camouflage.

1109
01:32:01,991 --> 01:32:03,868
There's a natural precedent.

1110
01:32:04,077 --> 01:32:07,580
Hungry predators
will avoid diseased bodies.

1111
01:32:08,039 --> 01:32:10,625
Equipped with the right pathogen,
our troops

1112
01:32:10,708 --> 01:32:12,961
would be essentially
invisible to the enemy.

1113
01:32:14,045 --> 01:32:17,048
You understand the only way
to prove this theory of yours is

1114
01:32:17,590 --> 01:32:18,967
for some idiot to infect themselves

1115
01:32:19,050 --> 01:32:20,927
with a lethal pathogen and then...

1116
01:32:22,178 --> 01:32:25,056
...meet with her, face to face.

1117
01:32:28,393 --> 01:32:29,519
Yes.

1118
01:32:30,186 --> 01:32:32,272
Do we have what we need to try it?

1119
01:32:32,355 --> 01:32:33,565
We have all he could want.

1120
01:32:34,315 --> 01:32:36,901
Typhus, H1N1, SARS.

1121
01:32:37,527 --> 01:32:39,195
The problem is,

1122
01:32:39,279 --> 01:32:41,281
they're all stored in B-Wing.

1123
01:32:42,240 --> 01:32:43,992
What's the matter with B-Wing?

1124
01:32:45,493 --> 01:32:48,580
Dr. Spellman.
Our chief vaccinologist.

1125
01:32:49,956 --> 01:32:52,709
Within hours of the outbreak,
he'd been sent blood samples

1126
01:32:52,792 --> 01:32:54,961
to try and isolate the pathogenic cause.

1127
01:32:58,840 --> 01:33:00,341
Unfortunately...

1128
01:33:04,888 --> 01:33:06,222
This is B-Wing now.

1129
01:33:13,188 --> 01:33:14,981
God damn it.

1130
01:33:19,235 --> 01:33:20,486
How many?

1131
01:33:21,362 --> 01:33:22,530
How many are there?

1132
01:33:22,614 --> 01:33:24,449
There were 80 people working there.

1133
01:33:29,120 --> 01:33:30,955
I've never seen them move like that.

1134
01:33:31,039 --> 01:33:32,290
They're dormant.

1135
01:33:32,790 --> 01:33:34,792
They're awaiting stimulus.

1136
01:33:35,919 --> 01:33:36,961
Now, this

1137
01:33:38,004 --> 01:33:39,464
is vault 139.

1138
01:33:40,006 --> 01:33:41,799
That's where your samples would be.

1139
01:33:43,051 --> 01:33:45,428
This is the skybridge.

1140
01:33:46,679 --> 01:33:49,015
That connects B-Wing
to the main building here.

1141
01:33:49,974 --> 01:33:54,270
And this, is the only thing
standing between us and the skybridge.

1142
01:33:54,437 --> 01:33:55,480
SO,

1143
01:33:57,315 --> 01:33:59,150
what do you propose, Mr. Lane?

1144
01:34:14,082 --> 01:34:15,750
You are not serious.

1145
01:34:15,833 --> 01:34:19,170
B-Wing's a maze.
They'll never make it back alone.

1146
01:34:19,712 --> 01:34:21,547
We don't even know
if his theory is correct.

1147
01:34:21,631 --> 01:34:24,550
Well, I know I'm not asking
one of you to take him there.

1148
01:34:27,011 --> 01:34:28,680
Each has its merits.

1149
01:34:33,476 --> 01:34:35,979
- Last resort.
- It's too loud.

1150
01:34:38,189 --> 01:34:39,357
Let's go.

1151
01:34:41,693 --> 01:34:43,069
Try not to kill one.

1152
01:34:44,862 --> 01:34:48,199
It only makes
the rest of them more aggressive.

1153
01:34:49,200 --> 01:34:50,368
Yeah.

1154
01:35:07,552 --> 01:35:08,970
You sure you want to do this?

1155
01:35:09,721 --> 01:35:11,848
Of course I'm not. Let's go.

1156
01:35:12,598 --> 01:35:13,725
Good luck.

1157
01:35:15,101 --> 01:35:16,728
See you all shortly.

1158
01:35:21,774 --> 01:35:23,067
Good luck.

1159
01:35:26,529 --> 01:35:30,408
If anything comes down this hall before
we do, you seal these doors for good.

1160
01:35:30,658 --> 01:35:32,618
- Understood?
- Okay.

1161
01:37:59,307 --> 01:38:00,641
There they are.

1162
01:38:40,598 --> 01:38:41,599
Go, go.

1163
01:38:57,281 --> 01:38:58,491
Hurry up, hurry up, hurry up.

1164
01:38:58,950 --> 01:39:00,117
Come on!

1165
01:39:23,057 --> 01:39:24,976
They're fine. They're fine.

1166
01:39:59,260 --> 01:40:00,595
Shit.

1167
01:40:23,993 --> 01:40:26,162
The vault we need is in 139.

1168
01:41:02,865 --> 01:41:04,033
Go!

1169
01:41:08,537 --> 01:41:09,872
Oh, my God.

1170
01:41:16,212 --> 01:41:17,713
Left, left, left!

1171
01:41:19,423 --> 01:41:20,758
What are you doing?

1172
01:41:21,092 --> 01:41:22,593
She'll get you to the vault.

1173
01:42:39,712 --> 01:42:40,963
That's the vault.

1174
01:42:41,046 --> 01:42:42,381
- We can make it.
- No, we can't.

1175
01:42:44,675 --> 01:42:46,302
We can't make it. Let's go!

1176
01:43:11,911 --> 01:43:12,953
They're not gonna make it.

1177
01:43:13,037 --> 01:43:14,622
You heard what Javi said,
we cannot open it.

1178
01:43:14,705 --> 01:43:16,040
They're not alone, we can't open it!

1179
01:43:16,123 --> 01:43:17,500
They are coming back!

1180
01:43:19,543 --> 01:43:21,378
We can't leave them there.

1181
01:43:21,837 --> 01:43:22,922
Come on!

1182
01:43:25,716 --> 01:43:27,176
Open the door!

1183
01:43:29,678 --> 01:43:31,055
- Run!
- Run!

1184
01:43:31,222 --> 01:43:33,724
Run! Faster, come on!

1185
01:43:33,933 --> 01:43:35,017
Run!

1186
01:43:36,060 --> 01:43:37,686
In, in, in!

1187
01:43:44,068 --> 01:43:45,402
Come on!

1188
01:43:46,237 --> 01:43:48,072
Now where is Gerry?

1189
01:43:50,199 --> 01:43:52,535
Where is he, where is he, where is he?

1190
01:43:53,994 --> 01:43:56,163
Come on, come on, where are you?

1191
01:45:09,820 --> 01:45:11,572
DR. KELLY: 5-6-9-6-4.

1192
01:45:12,948 --> 01:45:15,200
5-6-9-6-4.

1193
01:45:44,188 --> 01:45:45,689
What happened to Gerry?

1194
01:45:59,703 --> 01:46:02,164
Not that one. Not that one.

1195
01:46:31,527 --> 01:46:32,653
Oh, shit!

1196
01:46:32,736 --> 01:46:33,821
Shit!

1197
01:46:56,301 --> 01:46:57,469
Jesus.

1198
01:46:58,220 --> 01:46:59,888
He's going to inject himself.

1199
01:47:06,145 --> 01:47:08,147
We have no idea
which one's going to work.

1200
01:47:08,230 --> 01:47:10,566
We don't know if any of them will work.

1201
01:47:11,191 --> 01:47:13,610
If he uses anything
he took from that left case,

1202
01:47:14,445 --> 01:47:15,946
he's dead anyway.

1203
01:47:41,638 --> 01:47:43,140
What's he doing?

1204
01:48:34,149 --> 01:48:35,984
How long does he have to wait?

1205
01:48:36,443 --> 01:48:38,987
Before he's infected? Not long, but,

1206
01:48:39,071 --> 01:48:41,698
that's not the question
we're really asking, is it?

1207
01:50:32,684 --> 01:50:34,019
Look at them.

1208
01:50:55,165 --> 01:50:56,792
He just walked right past him!

1209
01:51:02,714 --> 01:51:04,007
He walked right past him!

1210
01:51:04,800 --> 01:51:06,176
Like it was nobody!

1211
01:52:16,913 --> 01:52:17,914
Okay.

1212
01:53:06,004 --> 01:53:07,672
This isn't the end.

1213
01:53:17,474 --> 01:53:18,725
Not even close.

1214
01:53:18,809 --> 01:53:21,019
Hi, there. This Is...

1215
01:53:21,103 --> 01:53:22,687
This is Amy. Is anyone out there?

1216
01:53:22,771 --> 01:53:24,606
Hello. I'm trying
to get in contact with anyone.

1217
01:53:24,689 --> 01:53:26,775
We've had some luck
finding people with this transmission.

1218
01:53:26,858 --> 01:53:28,443
We've lost entire cities.

1219
01:53:28,527 --> 01:53:30,862
When there's
no more people left to infect,

1220
01:53:30,946 --> 01:53:33,115
they go dormant. Whole cities are lost.

1221
01:53:33,198 --> 01:53:34,658
The World Health Organization

1222
01:53:34,741 --> 01:53:36,618
reports today that help may soon...

1223
01:53:36,701 --> 01:53:38,703
...@ hybridized meningitis strain

1224
01:53:38,787 --> 01:53:41,081
with components of smallpox and H1N1.

1225
01:53:41,164 --> 01:53:42,874
We still don't
know how it started.

1226
01:53:43,083 --> 01:53:44,584
The World Health
Organization has created

1227
01:53:44,668 --> 01:53:47,546
a vaccine that works
as a kind of camouflage,

1228
01:53:47,629 --> 01:53:51,091
making people who receive it
invisible to the infected.

1229
01:53:51,425 --> 01:53:52,634
We bought
ourselves some time.

1230
01:53:52,717 --> 01:53:55,137
Volunteer forces
are delivering the vaccine

1231
01:53:55,220 --> 01:53:57,222
to areas that have been cordoned off.

1232
01:53:57,305 --> 01:54:00,058
Distribution efforts
began in earnest on April 10th...

1233
01:54:00,142 --> 01:54:01,518
The importance
of getting the information

1234
01:54:01,601 --> 01:54:03,728
out to those still alive
within the quarantine...

1235
01:54:04,688 --> 01:54:06,398
But it's given us a chance.

1236
01:54:22,831 --> 01:54:24,666
If you can get to a colder area,

1237
01:54:24,749 --> 01:54:26,710
to higher ground,
they move slower on the ground.

1238
01:54:26,877 --> 01:54:29,754
The Battle of Moscow is still raging.

1239
01:54:30,046 --> 01:54:32,883
Initial tests on the so-called camouflage

1240
01:54:32,966 --> 01:54:34,718
have been largely successful.

1241
01:54:39,598 --> 01:54:41,892
Others have found
a way to push back.

1242
01:54:42,726 --> 01:54:46,188
Move, move!
All right, juice 'em up!

1243
01:54:54,863 --> 01:54:57,199
Approaching target.
Permission to engage.

1244
01:54:57,532 --> 01:54:58,867
Permission granted.

1245
01:54:58,950 --> 01:55:01,453
All clear.
Light 'em up. Light 'em up.

1246
01:55:03,121 --> 01:55:04,414
It's permanent!

1247
01:55:04,498 --> 01:55:07,709
It's settled, it's settled! It's over with!

1248
01:55:07,792 --> 01:55:09,794
There's no forgiveness in hell!

1249
01:55:09,920 --> 01:55:13,507
Whatever goes to hell, stays in hell!

1250
01:55:13,882 --> 01:55:15,759
This is Station 7 in Nebraska,

1251
01:55:15,842 --> 01:55:16,968
broadcasting on the shortwave band.

1252
01:55:17,052 --> 01:55:19,679
If you can fight, fight.

1253
01:55:19,763 --> 01:55:20,931
Head north if you can.

1254
01:55:21,014 --> 01:55:23,975
Hello?
Is there anyone out there hearing this?

1255
01:55:24,059 --> 01:55:25,352
Help each other.

1256
01:55:25,435 --> 01:55:28,396
Mexico City has been
declared a complete loss.

1257
01:55:37,656 --> 01:55:39,449
Be prepared for anything.

1258
01:55:44,829 --> 01:55:46,831
Our war has just begun.

